Decorate the given method as cell magic.

The decorator can be used with or without arguments, as follows.

i) without arguments: it will create a cell magic named as the method being
decorated::

    @deco
    def foo(...)

will create a cell magic named `foo`.

ii) with one string argument: which will be used as the actual name of the
resulting magic::

    @deco('bar')
    def foo(...)

will create a cell magic named `bar`.

To register a class magic use ``Interactiveshell.register_magic(class or instance)``.

